# Release notes revision f (26 October 2026), built on revision e (2026-10-16, e1f7b8e9 as recorded in its inventory) by exact
# replacements, each asserted once. Adds PREREG46, the PREREG47 reading, the 14.2 arms on the Maine frames, the 1.9.0 DOI, the
# 1.10.0 staging, and the registration of PREREG48 and 14.3 PREREG2. Removes nothing. Usage: python3 build_rn_20261026f.py E F.
# No em dashes.
import sys
E, F = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
t = open(E, encoding="utf8").read(); w0 = len(t.split())
def one(a, b):
    global t
    assert t.count(a) == 1, (t.count(a), a[:90]); t = t.replace(a, b)

one("# FVS-ACD (AcadianGY) 14.2 refinement: release notes for PREREG16 to PREREG45b and the October 16 cross-version benchmark",
    "# FVS-ACD (AcadianGY) 14.2 refinement: release notes for PREREG16 to PREREG47 and the October 16 cross-version benchmark")
one("Draft of October 16, 2026 (revision e, built on the fourth revision of October 5, 2026)",
    "Draft of October 26, 2026 (revision f, built on revision e of October 16, 2026)")
one("The frozen 14.2 candidate arms p38_fit and qc_rh were not run in that benchmark, because their engine copies are on firebreather, which has been unreachable since October 11, 2026. For the same reason PREREG46 and revisions 1 to 5 of PREREG47 are registered but not yet run.",
    "The frozen 14.2 candidate arms p38_fit and qc_rh, run on its three Maine frames on October 26, 2026, reproduce 14.1 exactly, as both act only on Quebec heights.\n\n"
    "On October 26, 2026 two more QC studies ran, both for 14.3 only. PREREG46 tested a QC height increment multiplier with a zero in relative height and found no candidate: the form with its zero fixed at the measured maximum could not be fitted with a declining multiplier, and the linear form fitted its zero at 1.64 times ESI, past every measured stand, its held out increment ratio near the frontier is 1.341 with an interval too wide to bound, and, like PREREG45, lets top height rise past the frontier over 100 years. The PREREG47 reading of absolute Bakuzis gates on the measured QC stand lists finds every arm read not credible over 100 years: 14.1 holds QC top height nearly flat after its first decades, and p38_fit, PREREG45 and the PREREG46 linear form all overshoot the measured frontier. 14.2 still keeps 0.111.")
one("but they were not run, since their engine copies are on firebreather.",
    "and on October 26, 2026 they were run on the same three frames (OSC Cardinal, jobs 15885111 to 15885113, the engine code copied from firebreather): every compared value of results, tree level predictions and trajectories equals 14.1 exactly.")
one("\n\nPREREG45b took the NB arm to stand level,",
    "\n\nPREREG46, for 14.3 only, tested two forms with a zero in relative height, fitted with the increment integrated over each tag's interval: qc_lz, max(0, a + b r), and qc_ez, exp(a + b r) times a taper to zero at r 1.285, the largest measured top height over ESI. qc_ez stopped at its fit: with the zero fixed at 1.285 the fold A estimating equations give b positive (a 0.4303, b 0.9219), a registered stop, so it was not run. qc_lz was run under three logged deviations that drop qc_ez from the chain. It fits a = 2.2292 and b = -1.3631 (bootstrap interval -2.062 to -0.729), so its zero is at r 1.635 and m is still 0.48 at the largest measured relative height. Every harness gate passes, the fold B pooled ratio is 1.047 and the published TOPHT bias +14.45% against +14.63%, but the predicted over observed ratio in the 1 to 1.25 relative height bin is 1.341, with a bootstrap upper limit of 2.680 against 1.50, so the two relative height bin gates registered for this study fail (Rule 2, not adopted). From the 36 measured stand lists its median top height over ESI reaches 1.285 at 100 years (1.182 with the ST2 engine offset removed, 19 of 36 stands over 1.175), and it adds Reineke flags, so no candidate is named.\n\n"
    "PREREG45b took the NB arm to stand level,")
one("and is still rising.\n",
    "and is still rising.\n\n"
    "PREREG47 set absolute gates for the same grid, registered before any threshold or PREREG46 long run output existed: gate C on the measured frontier, a credibility floor, early and late top height growth (MG, MGN, LG), top height monotonicity with thresholds from measured stands, strict site ordering and the PREREG44 relations. Its thresholds were computed once on October 26, 2026 (F_HT 9.52 m, S_HT 11 stands); the early growth floor MG_LO came out at -0.025 m yr⁻¹, so the early growth gates can fail only an arm whose top height shrinks. Every arm read fails Rule 2. 14.1 fails late growth, with 7 of 36 stands gaining in every 20 year window after year 21 and late window medians within 5 cm of zero. p38_fit (1.418), PREREG45 (1.205) and PREREG46 qc_lz (1.182, read blind) all fail gate C on the offset removed median against 1.175. Strict site ordering fails in every arm, qc141 in 3 of 6 cells and the others in 6 of 6.\n")
one("For 14.3, the relative height multiplier of PREREG45 passes every benchmark gate but is not cleared on long run grounds; its NB counterpart (PREREG45b) is not adopted.",
    "For 14.3, the relative height multiplier of PREREG45 passes every benchmark gate but is not cleared on long run grounds; its NB counterpart (PREREG45b) is not adopted. The zero form of PREREG46 names no candidate, and the PREREG47 reading finds no QC arm read credible on the long run.")
one("the next arm is a form with a zero or an asymptote. Stress tests confirm the reading (PREREG45 revision 2).",
    "the next arm was a form with a zero or an asymptote. Stress tests confirm the reading (PREREG45 revision 2). PREREG46 tested that arm and named no candidate, and PREREG47 finds a flat 14.1 and three alternatives that overshoot (a bracket that is an inference to test, since no arm passes), so the next QC study needs height increment data near the frontier or a shape constraint chosen from outside the tag set.")
one("- The QC stems deficit of about 24 points shared by every anchor arm (PREREG28).",
    "- The QC stems deficit of about 24 points shared by every anchor arm (PREREG28). PREREG48, which splits it into survivor mortality and ingrowth with frozen qc_rh as the second arm, was registered on October 26, 2026 and waits on firebreather.")
one("- The PREREG46 long runs and the PREREG47 reading of them (revisions 1 to 5 registered October 11 to 15, 2026), and the registration of PREREG48 and PREREG49 after them. Each waits on firebreather, which has been unreachable since October 11, 2026, since Cardinal lacks their frozen inputs, the p19_a0111 qc_c results among them.",
    "- PREREG49 (the NS survival step and an NS grid from measured stand lists) is drafted and registers after five server lookups on firebreather.")
one("- The frozen 14.2 candidate arms p38_fit and qc_rh on the cross-version benchmark Maine sets, expected to equal qc141 there, which were not run because their engine copies are on firebreather.\n",
    "")
one("- A 14.3 thinning response limited to partial removals, since 14.1 overstates biomass recovery after heavy removals by 1.39 Mg ha⁻¹ yr⁻¹ and after intermediate removals by 1.41 (cross-version benchmark).",
    "- A 14.3 thinning response limited to partial removals, since 14.1 overstates biomass recovery after heavy removals by 1.39 Mg ha⁻¹ yr⁻¹ and after intermediate removals by 1.41 (cross-version benchmark). 14.3 pre-registration 1 (October 18 to 19) adopted no eligibility rule; 14.3 pre-registration 2, which re-estimates the form of T, was registered on October 26, 2026 and has not run.")
one("and the commit after fc78b2be (the cross-version benchmark package, this revision e of the notes, the README status section and the VERSION_HISTORY Era 7 to 9 entries).",
    "c9ad8277 on branch `acdx-crossversion-20261016` (the cross-version benchmark package, revision e of the notes, the README status section and the VERSION_HISTORY Era 7 to 9 entries), and d06c68ed on branch `v142-p46p47-docs-20261026` (PREREG46, the PREREG47 reading, the 14.2 arms on the Maine frames and the 1.9.0 drivers, in `scripts/v14.2dev/2026-10-26/`); this revision f is in the commit after d06c68ed.")
one("Version 1.9.0, which adds PREREG45, PREREG45b, the stress tests and the fourth 5 October revision, is staged on firebreather with Aaron's approval but is unpublished, so it has no DOI yet, and the cross-version benchmark goes into the version after it.",
    "Version 1.9.0, which adds PREREG45, PREREG45b, the stress tests and the fourth 5 October revision, was published on October 26, 2026 as 10.5281/zenodo.23665173 (its record metadata carries the staging date, October 5). Version 1.10.0, which adds the cross-version benchmark, PREREG46, the PREREG47 reading and the 14.2 arms, is staged and not published.")
one("PREREG46 (md5 eb4b753d) and PREREG47 revisions 1 to 5 (7f64d22c, 6a77fa5f, 21a36a30, 4fa7aea1 and d93f3035) are registered in `p47/logs/prereg_md5.txt` of the session record, and `thresholds_p47.R` has not been run, so no PREREG47 threshold has been read.",
    "PREREG46 (md5 eb4b753d) and PREREG47 revisions 1 to 5 (7f64d22c, 6a77fa5f, 21a36a30, 4fa7aea1 and d93f3035) were registered before any of their runs; `thresholds_p47.R` wrote its thresholds (md5 e9609cfb) before the reading, and the PREREG46 assembly md5 (5d593fca) was recorded after a dry run and before the assembly. PREREG48 revision 1 (61ab907e) is registered on the laptop copy.")
one("1.8.0 DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.23168366\n", "1.8.0 DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.23168366\n\n1.9.0 DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.23665173\n")
one("| Diagnostic, no engine change; p38_fit and qc_rh not run |", "| Diagnostic, no engine change; p38_fit and qc_rh run October 26, identical to 14.1 |")
t = t.rstrip("\n") + "\n" + \
    "| PREREG46 | QC height increment multiplier with a zero in relative height (qc_lz, qc_ez), informs 14.3 only | No candidate: qc_ez fit stop (Rule 1); qc_lz not adopted (Rule 2), gate C and Reineke also fail | qc_lz zero at r 1.635; 1 to 1.25 bin ratio 1.341 (upper 2.680) | 2026-10-26_v142_qc-relht-zero-form_RESULT.md |\n" + \
    "| PREREG47 | Absolute Bakuzis gates on the measured QC stand lists, reading r1, informs 14.3 only | Every arm read not credible on the long run (Rule 2) | qc141 late growth 7 of 36; offset removed median 1.418, 1.205 and 1.182 for p38_fit, qc_rh and qc_lz against 1.175 | 2026-10-26_v142_qc-bakuzis-absolute_RESULT.md |\n"
assert chr(0x2014) not in t
open(F, "w", encoding="utf8").write(t)
print("words", w0, "->", len(t.split()))
